1. Definitions

"Licensor" means the copyright owner or owners of the Software.

"Software" means all source code, object code, documentation, applications,
packages, tools, scripts, assets, and other first-party materials contained in
the Hyperfocus repository or distributed from that repository with this
license. This includes, without limitation, the Hyperfocus engine, engine
editor, AI development harness, shared packages, and all other first-party
code in the repository. Software does not include materials expressly
identified as third-party materials or governed by separate license terms,
and does not include Your Independent Content.

"You" means the individual or legal entity exercising rights under this
license. "Your Group" means You and every entity that directly or indirectly
controls, is controlled by, or is under common control with You.

"Modification" means any work based on, incorporating, translating, or
modifying any part of the Software.

"Independent Content" means code, art, audio, writing, data, project files,
and other material that does not copy protectable expression from the
Software. Output produced by the Software is Independent Content unless that
output itself contains Software.

"Licensed Game" means an interactive software title whose primary purpose is
play or entertainment and that includes or uses the Software. A Licensed Game
does not include an Engine Offering.

"Related Releases" means ports, editions, downloadable content, expansions,
renamed releases, and substantially similar releases of the same Licensed
Game. Related Releases are treated as one Licensed Game for the threshold and
royalty calculation.

"Engine Offering" means software or a hosted service whose primary purpose is
to create, edit, build, execute, or host games and that contains the Software
or a Modification. A Licensed Game is not an Engine Offering merely because
it includes ordinary game-specific modding tools, a level editor for that
game, or a dedicated server for that game.

"Adjusted Game Revenue" means money actually received by Your Group from, or
collected on its behalf for, commercial exploitation of a Licensed Game,
including sales, licenses, subscriptions, paid access, downloadable content,
in-game purchases, advertising, sponsorships, crowdfunding tied to access or
delivery, and advances or minimum guarantees attributable to the Licensed
Game. Adjusted Game Revenue excludes refunds, chargebacks, separately stated
sales taxes or value-added taxes, and storefront or payment-processing fees.
Ordinary development, payroll, hosting, marketing, and other business costs
are not deductions. Revenue from all Related Releases and all members of Your
Group is aggregated. Non-USD receipts are converted to USD using a reasonable,
consistently applied exchange rate available when the money is received.

"Consideration" means money or anything else of material value.

