Subject to this license, the Licensor grants You a worldwide, non-exclusive
license to:

a. view, inspect, evaluate, study, reproduce, and privately or publicly fork
   the Software;

b. modify the Software and create Modifications;

c. use the Software and Modifications privately, internally, and for personal,
   educational, research, evaluation, hobby, charitable, or other
   non-commercial purposes;

d. create, reproduce, modify, publicly perform, publicly display, distribute,
   sell, license, and otherwise commercially exploit Licensed Games under
   Sections 3 and 4; and

e. distribute the Software or a Modification without Consideration under
   Section 5.

You may allow employees, contractors, publishers, distributors, hosting
providers, and platform operators to exercise these rights solely on Your
behalf or as needed to develop, operate, or distribute Your Licensed Game. You
remain responsible for their compliance when they exercise rights on Your
behalf. You may transfer this license with a Licensed Game or with substantially
all of the business or assets responsible for that Licensed Game if the
recipient agrees in writing to this license and You pay royalties accrued
before the transfer. No other sublicense or transfer is granted.

3. Licensed Games and Independent Content

You may keep a Licensed Game's source code and Independent Content private.
You are not required to disclose game-specific code, Modifications to the
Software used only in a Licensed Game, art, audio, writing, data, or other
Independent Content merely because You use the Software.

You own Your Independent Content. This license does not grant the Licensor any
ownership interest in it. You may use, export, convert, and migrate Your
Independent Content to another engine at any time.

If a release is changed so that it no longer contains or uses any Software or
Modification, money received from that fully migrated release after the
change is not Adjusted Game Revenue. Money received for older releases that
still contain or use the Software remains Adjusted Game Revenue. Accrued
royalties do not disappear when a game is migrated.

4. Game Revenue Royalty

Each Licensed Game receives a USD 50,000 royalty-free allowance in each
calendar year. You owe the Licensor a royalty equal to five percent (5%) only
of Adjusted Game Revenue above USD 50,000 for that Licensed Game in that
calendar year:

  Annual Royalty = 5% x max(0, Adjusted Game Revenue - USD 50,000)

No royalty or revenue report is required for a Licensed Game that does not
exceed USD 50,000 of Adjusted Game Revenue in a calendar year.

After a Licensed Game exceeds the allowance, You must report and pay quarterly
within 45 days after each calendar quarter ends. The amount due for a quarter
is the cumulative annual royalty through that quarter minus royalties already
paid for that year. You must provide a final annual statement within 45 days
after the calendar year ends.

Reports and payments must use the contact method or payment instructions the
Licensor publicly designates with the Software or provides to You in writing.
If no method is designated when payment becomes due, You must notify the
repository owner through a private contact channel and retain the amount due
until reasonable payment instructions are provided; the absence of published
instructions does not waive the royalty.

You must keep records reasonably sufficient to verify Adjusted Game Revenue
and royalties for three years after the applicable report. No more than once
per calendar year, the Licensor may have an independent auditor inspect those
records on reasonable notice, during normal business hours, and subject to
reasonable confidentiality obligations. The Licensor pays the audit cost
unless the audit finds an underpayment greater than five percent (5%) for the
period examined, in which case You must pay the reasonable audit cost as well
as the underpayment.

The Licensor and You may replace or modify the royalty, reporting, or other
commercial terms through a separate written agreement.

5. Free Software Redistribution; No Monetized Software Forks

You may distribute the Software or a Modification only without Consideration
and only if You:

a. provide the complete corresponding source code at no charge;

b. include this license and keep all copyright and attribution notices;

c. identify material modifications; and

d. license the distributed Software or Modification under these same terms.

Without a separate written agreement from the Licensor, You may not sell,
license, rent, paywall, or charge for access to the Software, a Modification,
or an Engine Offering. You also may not condition access to them on buying
support, hosting, a subscription, another product, or another service.

This restriction does not prohibit charging for bona fide consulting,
training, support, hosting, or development services when access to the
Software or Modification remains available without charge and the fee is for
the service rather than a disguised Software license. It also does not
prohibit commercial Independent Content, plugins, libraries, or tools that
interoperate with the Software but do not contain Software or a Modification.

